license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"          # <- bump to whatever tag you push with the twin
date-released: "2026-07-25"   # <- set to the actual release date
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21464028
keywords:
  - Herculaneum
  - papyrology
  - Vesuvius Challenge
  - virtual unwrapping
  - structural metrics
  - synthetic ground truth
abstract: >-
  ML-independent structural tools for Herculaneum scroll
  surfaces: a topological grid metric that measures the
  scribe's writing lattice without reading text, a
  void-aware layer-count reconciliation, and a synthetic
  scroll twin that sizes itself from the length of the work,
  crushes to the measured deformation, and supplies
  per-letter ground truth for testing the toolchain. Every
  mode ships with the pre-registered acceptance test that
  gates it.
